- **Structure:** after the account loads, the router states the debt and asks "Can you make this payment today?". From there the customer goes either to `negotiate`, which holds all the amount, date, persuasion and recording rules, or to one of the six specialist nodes. `negotiate` tells the model to offer exactly the `offer_instead` value whenever a result has one.
- **Change to the extracted situations:** I didn't give the router a direct route to `refused`. A customer can only use up their persuasion attempts in `negotiate`, so `refused` is reached from there.
- **Gap:** I didn't get to step 7, the rule-by-rule re-read of the brief against the workflow.

The workflow is in `out/w3-A2.workflow.json` and the generator is `out/w3-A2.gen.py`. The brief and the date facts agreed, so I followed both as given.

